1
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,840
YAMU!

2
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,640
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,317
YAMU!

4
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,800
YAMU!

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

6
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:05,733
Man, this has got to be the
closest match I've ever seen.

7
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,180
Me too.

8
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:13,499
With just 50 life points separating
their scores, it's anyone's game.

9
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,993
Don't let up now, Joey.

10
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,860
It all comes down to these next few turns.

11
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,637
Your sister's counting on you.

12
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:20,602
Make her proud.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:21,940
No crap.

14
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,720
This duel has turned into
quite the nail-biter.

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,720
Joey, a virtual unknown going card for
card with the Intercontinental Champion?

16
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:34,780
I wonder what it is that fuels
these splendid performances.

17
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:38,201
Perhaps my Millennium Eye
will show me the answer.

18
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,360
Ah, yes, of course.

19
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:46,468
Keith has been wading in a pool of misery
ever since that defeat I handed him.

20
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,620
Now he's seeking his revenge.

21
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,160
As for Joey...

22
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:55,517
These markings are a
symbol of our friendship

23
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,097
and how we'll always be
there for one another.

24
00:01:58,180 --> 00:01:59,460
And a sister?

25
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,320
My, my.

26
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,400
So while one is driven
by bitter vengeance,

27
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:08,440
the other is motivated by love and trust.

28
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:11,860
Why, it's practically a
battle of good versus evil.

29
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,200
How amusing.

30
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:20,460
Come on, let's get on
with this matcha, dweeb.

31
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:24,037
I got plenty more machine
monsters all revved up

32
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:27,020
and ready to totally
steamroll your life points.

33
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:33,700
Yeah, you ain't nothing but a speed
bump on my way to duel Pegasus.

34
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:37,391
And that goes double for that
dweeby friend of yours, Yugi.

35
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,260
Yeah, right, Keith.

36
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,162
What'd you say?

37
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,987
I got news for you, pal,
even if you beat me.

38
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,620
Which you won't. Yugi'd cream you.

39
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,680
And you know why, Hotshot?

40
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,237
Because you're a selfish
sleazeball who's only

41
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:54,720
in this tournament for your
own greedy reasons. Say what?

42
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:57,137
People like you never win.

43
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,900
Sure, your tricks may
get you a little ways,

44
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,320
but only till people with
good intentions show up.

45
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:07,080
Like me, and like Yu-Gi, too. Oh, yeah?

46
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,460
We'll just see about that.

47
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:13,280
One card face down, and
I'll attack with this.

48
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:20,199
My barrel dragon is gonna blast you
and your good intentions to dust.

49
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:24,080
See, with its triple attack
laser discharge system,

50
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:26,217
it has three attacks, not just one.

51
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,877
I can clear all your monsters
from the field in just one turn.

52
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:30,790
What?

53
00:03:30,873 --> 00:03:31,703
Three attacks?

54
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:32,740
That's right.

55
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,240
You're going down.

56
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:37,580
So say adios to your two
buddies on the field.

57
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,760
Go, proton blast!

58
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,380
That thing totaled them both.

59
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:56,000
That's what a 2,600-point
attack will do for you. Face it.

60
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,418
This is the end of the line for you.

61
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:03,340
No monster you got is gonna be able
to withstand this kind of firepower.

62
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,160
No wonder Keith was acting so confidently.

63
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:08,580
Just look at that thing.

64
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,487
Joey really has his work
cut out for him now.

65
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,252
Are you done yet, Keith?

66
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:17,785
Cause I already figured out how
to beat you, little toy blaster.

67
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:23,100
Meet the master of the past and future.

68
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,817
The time wizard.

69
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,220
Oh, right!

70
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,481
That could work!

71
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:32,677
Yeah, if that time roulette lands right,
that machine monster will age and corrode.

72
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,172
And I'm not done, Keith.

73
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,301
I'm throwing this baby down, too.

74
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,320
Baby dragon, that is.

75
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,567
Now you got two things
to worry about, Keith.

76
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:46,680
That blaster of yours rustin' up
and this little guy growin' up.

77
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,940
Let's do it!

78
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,720
Go, time roulette!

79
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,497
Of course, if that time
roulette lands wrong,

80
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,617
then Joey will have
something to worry about.

81
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:59,037
His Time Wizard will be destroyed and
he'll be at the mercy of Keith's blaster.

82
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,940
It's in fate's hands now.

83
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,760
Come on, Joey.

84
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,276
We're with you, bud.

85
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,640
Come on, Time Wizard.

86
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:18,526
I really need you to
come through for me here.

87
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,477
It's slowing down.

88
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:24,680
Don't land on a skull.

89
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,440
Get there.

90
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,580
All right, yeah!

91
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,640
Go Time Wizard!

92
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,760
Check it out.

93
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,617
Time magic is causing
Keith's dragon to rust up.

94
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:47,759
He's losing power.

95
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,960
While Joey's dragon is
gaining power as it evolves.

96
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,141
Nice work, Joey!

97
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,160
The stage is set perfectly!

98
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,960
Now, Thousand Dragon!

99
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:59,000
Noxious Nostril Gust!

100
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:03,980
Got him.

101
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,925
That hunk of steel is history.

102
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:10,020
But history repeats itself.

103
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,537
Especially when you're
taking on a deck that's

104
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:15,297
stacked with all kinds of
different machine cards.

105
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:17,220
Like this trap, for example.

106
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:18,980
A trap card?

107
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,980
Say hello to my
time-travelin' time machine.

108
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,240
Oh, what's in that chamber?

109
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:32,740
My time machine can travel
back in time one turn.

110
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:35,180
This can't be good.

111
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:38,536
So I can retrieve the monster
that you just destroyed.

112
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:40,880
It's his barrel dragon again.

113
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:43,820
It's back, and it looks
brand spanking new.

114
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:48,300
All of its point totals have
gone back to full power.

115
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,820
Go, proton blast!

116
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,200
He's gone.

117
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,960
My dragon's gone.

118
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:02,980
And he's gonna stay gone, too.

119
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:07,257
That is, unless you have a time
machine trap set up to bring him back.

120
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:11,520
But then he'd be coming back a
baby dragon, wouldn't he? Huh?

121
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:14,060
What are you talking about? Oh, right,

122
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:17,817
because the time machine brings back your
monster the way it was one turn before.

123
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:21,057
And since Keith's monster didn't
rust over until this turn,

124
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,375
it came back the way it was last turn.

125
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,345
Unfazed by Joey's time wizard.

126
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,650
Punk,

127
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:28,397
I knew you were gonna
use that dweeby little

128
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,920
time wizard to try and rust up my dragon.

129
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:34,945
You forget, I saw every card in
your deck when you dueled bones.

130
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,382
Duels are more than just
about the cards you use.

131
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:41,740
Yeah, they're about backbone too.

132
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:45,877
And judging from the look on your face
when my dragon came back through time,

133
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,000
I'd say you don't even have one.

134
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,380
Now make your move.

135
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,080
I'll throw a monster in defense mode.

136
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,920
And that's it.

137
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:57,817
That's it is right, because my
machines are going to keep on coming.

138
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,180
Go slot machine!

139
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,320
Attack mode!

140
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:03,880
Now your turn, dragon.

141
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:06,413
Blast that defense card to kingdom come!

142
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:08,000
Proton blast!

143
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:16,377
I could throw a monster out and
destroy Keith's slot machine,

144
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:20,217
but then he'd just turn around and destroy
whatever card I play with that dragon.

145
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:25,140
Even my strongest card of all, the red-eyes
black dragon, wouldn't stand a chance.

146
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,160
Poor Joey.

147
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:28,860
He's in a tough bind.

148
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,940
Joey, believe in your cards!

149
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:34,257
You need to trust them if
you're gonna beat that thing!

150
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:35,170
Hmm.

151
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:42,677
I'm going to lay one
card face down and throw

152
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:45,172
the Red-Eyes Black Dragon in attack mode.

153
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,700
And that'll do it for me.

154
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:56,257
That Red-Eyes Dragon may be the best
card you've got in your entire deck,

155
00:08:56,340 --> 00:09:00,360
dweeb, but he's still no match
for this kind of blasted power.

156
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:06,200
Say bye-bye to your prized possession.

157
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,200
Proton blast attack!

158
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:10,980
Not so fast.

159
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:12,820
What's that?

160
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,254
It's a little something called copycat.

161
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:18,580
It lets me copy one card that you've used.

162
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,240
And I'm choosing to
copy Magic Metal Force.

163
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:28,740
Now my red-eyes black dragon is
a red-eyes black metal dragon.

164
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:35,660
And that makes him strong
enough to withstand your attack.

165
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:44,220
All right, now Keith's
dragon is the one in trouble.

166
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:48,480
Red eyes, counterattack,
flash, flare, blast.

167
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,560
How do you like that, Keith?

168
00:09:55,840 --> 00:10:00,777
Your triple blast dragon machine has been
reduced to a pile of smoking metal debris.

169
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:05,880
And with my sister's sight on the line,
I plan on getting even tougher on you.

170
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,480
Check it out.

171
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,337
Since Keith's dragon's gone,

172
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:19,457
Joey's Metal Red Eyes is the
toughest card in the block.

173
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:21,437
Yeah, but don't count Keith out yet.

174
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,897
There must be some reason he
played that slot machine monster.

175
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:28,745
I knew you were an amateur, and
now I'm gonna show you how come.

176
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:31,900
Huh? Amateur?

177
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:36,500
Um, didn't I just go and blast
your best monster to bits?

178
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:37,890
That's right.

179
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:39,512
Keep talking, tough guy.

180
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,437
I'm laying this card face down,

181
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:45,049
and I'm switching my slot machine
monster to defensive mode.

182
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,020
Boy, is Keith losing it?

183
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:51,097
That slot machine can't take a blast from
my red eyes no matter what mode he's in.

184
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:53,017
Guess I'll have to learn the hard way.

185
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,260
Bad move, Chief.

186
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:59,820
First, I'll lay this face down, And now,
my red eyes will attack. Flash! Flare!

187
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:00,830
Blast!

188
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,784
Man, you're as predictable
as you are brainless.

189
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:06,876
I'm playing the card I had face down.

190
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:08,680
Go, seven completed!

191
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:10,750
Huh?

192
00:11:10,833 --> 00:11:13,600
How come that middle slot
just switched to a seven?

193
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,300
He's still there?

194
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,294
That's because my seven completed card
raises my slot's defensive points.

195
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:26,400
To 3,000 to be exact.

196
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,637
And that's more than
enough to deflect your

197
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,132
Red-Eyes Black Dragon's strongest attack.

198
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:36,000
And because my attack is lower than
its defense, I lose life points.

199
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:38,340
Man, this stinks.

200
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:42,420
That Flash Flare Blast is the
strongest attack Joey has, too.

201
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,366
And you know what else I got?

202
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:47,140
Two more seven completed cards in my deck,

203
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:51,340
each able to power up my slot's
defense or attack by 700 points.

204
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:55,877
Yeah, well, just because you have them
doesn't mean you'll draw them, Keith.

205
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:58,280
Oh, I ain't too worried about that.

206
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,520
Well, what do you know?

207
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,602
Check out what card I just drew.

208
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:09,800
I think I'll go ahead
and take it for a spin.

209
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,340
This time for my attack power.

210
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,780
Oh, man.

211
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:18,757
If I don't do something soon, my life
points are gonna get cleaned out.

212
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,670
Oh, no.

213
00:12:19,753 --> 00:12:22,617
One more of those seven completed
cards and that slot will

214
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,577
have powered up enough to
destroy Joey's Red-Eyes Dragon.

215
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,778
And then the other card he has, too.

216
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,660
Next, I'm throwing this down.

217
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,280
Go, Blast Sphere!

218
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:35,180
And attach yourself to Joey's Dragon.

219
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:39,970
Huh?

220
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:41,840
Blast Sphere? That's right.

221
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:44,477
And once I end my turn,
it'll self-destruct,

222
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:47,442
giving off 2,900 points
of damage to your dragon.

223
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,560
Self-destruct?

224
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:50,217
Oh, no!

225
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:53,947
Oh, and I thought I just had
that slot machine to worry about.

226
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:57,680
Okay, dweeb.

227
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,720
I'm ending my turn now.

228
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,200
Your time's up.

229
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:07,840
Blammo, ha!

230
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,280
But that dragon should be blown to bits.

231
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:17,920
This ain't right.

232
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,500
Oh, it's right.

233
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,580
Thanks to my handy Dragon Nails card,

234
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,880
it made my red eyes 600
attack points stronger.

235
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,680
Of course, the blast got deflected.

236
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:31,500
You dweeb, now my life points go down.

237
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:33,526
Oh, you're gonna make me cry.

238
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,266
I'll make you cry, all right.

239
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,860
Just you wait.

240
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:42,680
Well, looky what I got here.

241
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,680
I think I'll power up
my slot's attack again.

242
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,420
Well, would you look at that?

243
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:56,017
Both their monsters have
the same attack points now.

244
00:13:56,100 --> 00:14:00,677
And Joey and Keith have almost the exact
same amount of life points remaining, too.

245
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:03,348
This next turn could
decide the whole match.

246
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,860
The shield and sword card.

247
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:09,717
Playing this would swap all monsters'
defense points with their attack points,

248
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:11,624
but that'd only help Keith out.

249
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:18,300
Come on, no card you play's gonna help.

250
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:19,538
Just end your turn.

251
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,390
Thanks.

252
00:14:21,473 --> 00:14:24,600
Now, I think I'll go ahead
and end this duel. Huh?

253
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,014
It's all over for you.

254
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,120
Thanks to this.

